# Every text file is LF in the working tree, on every machine.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true`, which checks text out as CRLF. The suite reads its
# own source with `include_str!` and matches on "\n" (the release-commit guard in
# screens/dashboards.rs, and a dozen more), and the log fixtures are measured byte for byte, so a
# default Windows clone would be red before a contributor touched anything. Pinning eol here wins
# over any user or system autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff2 binary
